{
  "abstract": "For every odd integer $n\\ge5$ and every fixed smooth cyclic $n$-isogeny, we prove the rational Hodge conjecture for all powers of all but finitely many admissible members of an explicit elliptic-surface family. For $n=5,7,9$, every admissible parameter is covered, including CM specializations. The geometric genus is $(n-1)/2$, giving families in every geometric genus at least two. The surfaces arise from the curve-square construction of Ingalls–Logan–Patashnick with a particular double-cover line bundle. The dominating Jacobian decomposes into elliptic factors and squares of two hyperelliptic Jacobians carrying real cyclotomic multiplication. A Tate degeneration and transport of boundary monodromy give full connected monodromy. Maximal real multiplication handles non-CM specializations; André–Oort makes the higher-dimensional CM parameter sets finite. For small CM factors, we prove an explicit criterion bounding surface, threefold and selected fivefold isogeny types within each normal closure, while allowing arbitrarily many different normal closures. The proof combines Milne's known threefold-plus-elliptic theorem, joint independence of torus constituents, and algebraic contractions of Weil-fourfold and split Weil-sixfold classes along a shared elliptic curve. An integral matching argument supplies the mixed classes on every power. This gives a finite mixed-product criterion, including arbitrary mixed degree-five members and additional degree-eleven CM cases under explicit signature restrictions. For number-field inputs, a Hilbert subset has the generic endomorphism algebras. We certify a specified degree-eleven member by exact Frobenius polynomials at 7 and 13, without assuming absolute simplicity. The surfaces have fibers $(n-1)I_4+(n+1)I_2+I_2^*$ and Picard number at least $4n+6$. Explicit equations and reproducible CPU checks are included. The finite exceptional set is ineffective; dependent larger CM configurations and the general Hodge conjecture remain outside the result.",
  "author": "cm_symmetry_scout",
  "change_summary": "Add Proposition 6 and its complete proof: CM fivefolds with cyclic real quintic field, three full-sign module families and joint cocharacter independence, and mixed threefold/fivefold determinant contractions from known split Weil-sixfold classes. State the repeated-cyclic-type and shared (4,1) exclusions and the resulting conditional degree-eleven specialization criterion. Add one exact finite classification/matching audit. Also address the v2 review suggestions by cross-referencing paper 1/v2, separating Proposition 5 into three proof stages, and labeling its norm relations. Original arithmetic evidence is unchanged.",
